<title>UK: Summary of new CBI UK economic forecasts.</title>
<headline>Summary of new CBI UK economic forecasts.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-02-20</dateline>
<text>
<p>Following is a summary of revised forecasts of British economic indicators by the Confederation of British Industry (CBI), published Thursday. (Annual percentage changes unless otherwise stated) (figures in brackets are the CBI's last forecasts, published in December):</p>
<p>					  1997	   1998</p>
<p> Total GDP			   2.8 (3.1)    2.6</p>
<p> Manufacturing output	    2.5 (3.4)    2.9</p>
<p> Consumer expenditure	    4.1 (4.3)    3.4</p>
<p> Fixed investment		  5.3 (5.8)    5.1</p>
<p> of which General government  -7.1 (-7.2)  -5.1</p>
<p> Manufacturing		     5.4 (8.1)    8.5</p>
<p> Private Dwellings		 5.2 (5.6)    3.2</p>
<p> Other				 8.4 (8.6)    7.2</p>
<p> Government consumption	  0.9 (0.8)    0.8</p>
<p> Exports(goods/services)	 3.9 (4.6)    4.6</p>
<p> Imports(goods/services)	 6.5 (6.8)    5.7</p>
<p> Current account (bln stg)    -4.8(-6.7)   -5.4</p>
<p> Stockbuilding (blns stg)	2.5 (2.2)    1.9</p>
<p> Inflation (RPI) (Q4)	    2.5 (3.0)    3.0</p>
<p> RPIX (Q4)			   2.2 (2.5)    2.7</p>
<p> Unemployment (millions)	 1.64(1.71)   1.59</p>
<p> Company profits*		  5.9 (6.9)    4.5</p>
<p> PSBR (blns stg)**		22.2 (21.3)  17.8</p>
<p> PSBR as % of GDP		  2.8 (2.7)    2.1</p>
<p>* Company profits are gross pre-tax trading profits of industrial and commercial companies, net of stock appreciation and excluding North Sea oil, and adjusted for inflation as measured by the GDP deflator.</p>
<p>RPIX is retail prices excluding mortgage interest payments.</p>
<p>** PSBR data are for fiscal years.</p>
<p>-- Rosemary Bennett, London Newsroom +44-171-542 7715</p>
</text>
